Collapse sidebar and open default notebook on startup

Controlled by two independent env vars:
- VSCODE_COLLAPSE_SIDEBAR: collapse the primary sidebar after workbench startup
- VSCODE_OPEN_DEFAULT_NOTEBOOK: suppress Welcome and open a top-level .ipynb

Both flags are gated by truthy values (1 or true, case-insensitive).
When notebook flag is on, scan the workspace folder for *.ipynb files,
pick one at random, set defaultLayout to force-open it, and set
workbench.startupEditor to none. When sidebar flag is on, collapse the
sidebar via IWorkbenchLayoutService after startup. Flags are independent.
